# __PLUGIN_NAME__

__DESCRIPTION__

Registers one DeepSeek Harness tool, `__TOOL_NAME__`.

## Layout

```
src/index.ts        name / inject / Config / apply(ctx, config) + the tool definition
src/config.ts       Schemastery Config (interface + runtime schema, same name)
cordis.patch.yml    the profile layer this package contributes (row id: __PLUGIN_ID__)
test/logic.test.mjs node --test suite, importing from ../dist/*.js
dist/               build output -- git-ignored, but REQUIRED before install
```

## Build

```bash
npm install
npm run build            # rebuild after EVERY source edit: the install is a symlink
npm test
```

## Install into a profile

There is no `dsh` on PATH; invoke the CLI by path.

```bash
# `~` does NOT expand inside double quotes -- use $HOME.
# The handle holds the PATH only: bin.js is the declared `bin` and runs on its own.
# `DSH="node $HOME/..."` would break `$DSH ...` under zsh, which does not word-split.
DSH="$HOME/.dsh/profiles/node_modules/@deepseek-ai/dsh/lib/bin.js"

cd ..                                              # the directory CONTAINING this package
$DSH plugin --profile web add -w ./__PLUGIN_NAME__ # -w is MANDATORY for `add`
$DSH --profile web --dump-config | grep -A6 '__PLUGIN_NAME__'
```

`add` mutates `~/.dsh/profiles/web/package.json` twice: pnpm adds an absolute `link:` dependency,
and dsh appends `__PLUGIN_NAME__` to `dsh.profile.bundles`. `cordis.yml` is never touched.

## Configure

Per-profile overrides go in `~/.dsh/profiles/<p>/cordis.patch.yml`, keyed on the row `id`:

```yaml
- id: __PLUGIN_ID__
  config:
    defaultMode: lower
    maxLength: 4000        # a patch REPLACES `config` wholesale -- restate every key
```

Disable without uninstalling:

```yaml
- id: __PLUGIN_ID__
  disabled: true
```

Only the two USER-layer patch files hot-reload: `~/.dsh/profiles/<p>/cordis.patch.yml` and
`~/.dsh/cordis.patch.yml`. This package's own `cordis.patch.yml`, a rebuilt `dist/`, and bundle
membership changes all need a profile restart -- module HMR is disabled in both stock profiles.

## Uninstall

```bash
$DSH plugin --profile web remove __PLUGIN_NAME__   # no -w; remove by PACKAGE NAME
```

## Version pinning

`devDependencies` are pinned to the versions the profile actually runs. Re-check after a dsh
upgrade:

```bash
for p in cordis dsh-tools schemastery; do
  echo -n "$p: "
  node -p "require(require('os').homedir()+'/.dsh/profiles/node_modules/@deepseek-ai/$p/package.json').version"
done
```

Never use `"*"` in `devDependencies`: npm's `latest` dist-tag for `@deepseek-ai/dsh-tools` points at
an older, incompatible API line.
